## 1. General Security Hardening

| Issue | Why it matters | Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|----------------|
| **No HTTP security headers** | Browsers can be tricked into XSS, click‑jacking, MIME‑sniffing, etc. | Add **helmet** middleware (`npm i helmet`). |
| **No rate limiting** | Brute‑force, DoS, and credential‑stuffing attacks are possible on any endpoint. | Use **express‑rate‑limit** (or similar). |
| **Port is hard‑coded** | Makes it harder to run the app in different environments and may expose the process if the default port is already in use. | Read the port from `process.env.PORT` with a fallback. |
| **Uncaught errors will crash the process** | A single thrown error can bring the whole service down. | Add a global error‑handling middleware and process‑level listeners (`process.on('uncaughtException')`, `process.on('unhandledRejection')`). |
| **No request body parser** (even though the current routes are GET‑only) | Future POST/PUT routes would accept raw bodies, potentially leading to malformed data or injection. | Add `express.json()` (and optionally `express.urlencoded`) early in the middleware chain. |

### Quick implementation

```js
